Looking at this problem, I need to find either:
1. An independent set of size ⌈√n⌉, OR
2. A cycle of length at least ⌈√n⌉

A good approach is to use DFS to find cycles. When we find a back edge to an ancestor during DFS, we have a cycle. If the cycle is short, we continue and potentially fall back to finding an independent set using BFS coloring (where vertices at the same BFS level form an independent set).

